questions.prompt:
This invoice processing loop is O(N²). Identify the nested operation:
```js
function processInvoices(invoices, pricingTiers) {
  return invoices.map(inv => {
    const tier = pricingTiers.find(t => t.id === inv.tierId); // ← here
    return { ...inv, price: tier.price * inv.quantity };
  });
}
```

options:
Build a Map from tierId → tier BEFORE the loop, then look up in O(1) per invoice:
`const tierMap = new Map(pricingTiers.map(t => [t.id, t]));
return invoices.map(inv => ({ ...inv, price: tierMap.get(inv.tierId).price * inv.quantity }));`

